think Read the voice and style guides, REMEMBER, the three itineraries, and the top rows of session-logs/README.md. The live green edge is Season G open-media; the last lap landed image/label.rye (the 8-connected component labeler). The Microkernel double-seat leads Lindy yet its only ungated moves sit behind a web-fetch/license gate, surfaced not crossed -- so the agent-doable crux stays Season G.
think Standfast first: swept crux/REDS.md rows 80-87 -- all CLOSED/released/booked-as-own-round; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a gate, not agent-closable). Standfast clear, new work may open.
think The label log named three crux-first siblings: a DISTANCE TRANSFORM (the chamfer two-pass over a mask), a region/bounding-box reader over a LabelMap, a disk-element builder. Crux-first takes the hardest-solvable that opens the rest: the distance transform is a genuine two-pass algorithm and the most Lindy (the metric floor a distance-based erode/dilate, a watershed, and a shape-thickness reader all descend from), matching the pattern of taking the real algorithm over the reader/generator.
think Chose the canonical convention -- distance to the nearest BACKGROUND pixel, so the foreground grows inward and the field's local maxima trace the medial axis, the exact field skeleton/zhang_suen thin a shape down toward. The classic chamfer 3-4 (Borgefors, 1986): orthogonal step 3, diagonal 4, a forward raster pass over W/NW/N/NE and a backward reverse-raster pass over E/SE/S/SW. Integer, deterministic, no float, no sqrt -- squarely in the TAME happy zone.
think Compose not braid: this rung owns only the chamfer weights, the two-pass min-relaxation sweep (a `relax` helper), and the render ramp. branch.is_on reads the binary door (red >= 128), qoi owns the buffer, color.mix blends the colorize grayscale ramp. Bounded before a byte: dist_far = maxInt(u32)/2 sits far above any real chamfer distance (<= 4*8192 = 32768) yet leaves room to add a step weight without overflow; an empty source refuses by name having allocated nothing.
think Traced the crux values by hand before coding: a solid 3x3 block reads 3 around its ring (one orthogonal step from the edge) and 6 at its center (two steps); a pixel touching a lone background hole only at its CORNER reads 4 not 3 (the diagonal weight); the same hole at the BOTTOM-RIGHT is reached only on the backward pass -- the decisive proof the second pass is load-bearing.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds -- the hand-trace held. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living_docs_lint advisory-only, living_card_ascii_witness GREEN after the REMEMBER repoint.
obs Caught my own future-date: distance_version and the REMEMBER references read 20260818.140000 before the live clock (134545) was read; corrected both to the real clock per the REDS #75 lesson (measurement beats memory -- read the clock, never guess it).
obs Council rota lap deep-read item 24, active-designing/20260702-184312_the-grain-and-the-crossing.md -- the grain strands (bounded everything, values apart never braided, sameness as compression, witnesses first). Applied directly: the module names its ceiling up front, crosses no value into another whole, composes over the shared is_on/qoi/mix doors rather than duplicating them, and claims GREEN only on a witness on metal.
